Subject: [PATCH 1/2] freedreno/a3xx: program the pitch of a 4x4 tile row

A TILE_4X4 row contains four pixel rows. The allocation layout retains its
ordinary byte pitch per pixel row, but the hardware texture, resolve and
sysmem target pitches must address a full tile row. Convert at the a3xx
hardware boundary, including the mipmap pitch alignment. Leave the sysmem
bin width and allocation sizes in their original units.

On SM-T531/Adreno305b, the unmodified ttile path aliases x=320,y=0 with
x=0,y=4 on a 1280-pixel RGBA texture. A 257-pixel texture aliases at x=72
because its allocation pitch is aligned to 288 pixels. This change removes
that aliasing in full and partial-upload checks on both sizes. BGRA also
requires patch 2. Texture tiling is still opt-in; other GPU generations are
unchanged. Mipmapped/array/depth workloads and other a3xx GPUs need further
hardware validation before enabling this policy by default.

Base: Mesa25.0.7, https://archive.mesa3d.org/mesa-25.0.7.tar.xz
Archive-SHA256: 592272df3cf01e85e7db300c449df5061092574d099da275d19e97ef0510f8a6
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_resource.h b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_resource.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_resource.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_resource.h
@@ -14,4 +14,13 @@
 uint32_t fd3_setup_slices(struct fd_resource *rsc);
 unsigned fd3_tile_mode(const struct pipe_resource *tmpl);
 
+/* A 4x4 tiled pitch addresses one four-row tile strip. Keep allocation
+ * layout pitches in bytes per pixel row; convert only hardware pitches.
+ */
+static inline uint32_t
+fd3_resource_pitch(struct fd_resource *rsc, unsigned level)
+{
+   return fd_resource_pitch(rsc, level) * (rsc->layout.tile_mode ? 4 : 1);
+}
+
 #endif /* FD3_RESOURCE_H_ */
